==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|abandoned}}, equivalent to {{af|en|abandon|-ed}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əˈbæn.dənd/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/əˈbæn.dənd/|a=GenAm}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-abandoned.ogg|a=US}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Having given oneself up to [[vice]]; [[immoral]]; [[extremely]] wicked, or [[sinning]] without restraint; [[irreclaimably]] wicked. {{defdate|First attested from 1350 to 1470}}<ref name=SOED>{{R:SOED5|page=2}}</ref>
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:evil}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1876|author=Alexander Davidson|title=A Complete History of Illinois from 1673 to 1884|page=232|passage=Such immunity to offenders offered a safe asylum to the vilest and most '''abandoned''' scoundrels.}}
# No longer maintained by its former owners, residents{{,}} or caretakers; [[forsaken]], [[deserted]]. {{defdate|Late 15th century}}<ref name =SOED/>
#: {{syn|en|careless|deserted|discarded|forsaken|Thesaurus:abandoned}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1735|author=Thomson|passage={{...}} your '''abandoned''' streams {{...}}}}
# Free from constraint; [[uninhibited]]. {{defdate|Late 17th century}}<ref name =SOED/>
#: {{syn|en|dissolute}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1919|author=[[w:William Somerset Maugham|W. Somerset Maugham]]|title=w:The Moon and Sixpence|chapter=11|passage=Everything was dirty and [[shabby]]. There was no sign of the '''abandoned''' luxury that Colonel MacAndrew had so confidently described.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=4 Feb 84|volume=11|number=28|journal=Gay Community News|page=14|author=M. S.|title=''Celles qui aiment:'' The Lesbians of Montreal|text=What is the same is our need for community. What seemed different was an '''abandoned''' enjoyment of life and music, a uniquely Quebec sense of ''joie de vivre''.}}
# {{lb|en|geology}} No longer being acted upon by the geologic forces that formed it.

